Subject: [PATCH 2/5] M1: staff sign in, sign out and password change

Build api/v1/auth.php actions login, logout and change_password. Login
validates CSRF, rate limits by IP and by identifier, treats the identifier as
email when it contains "@" else phone, verifies against users.password_hash,
checks the account is active, regenerates the session id, sets the user id,
loads the RBAC set and records last_login_at, then returns a JSON redirect to
/admin for staff. A plain form post gets a real redirect, so it works without
JavaScript. An unknown identifier costs the same time as a real one, and no
exception ever reaches the client.

Wire admin/login.php with assets/js/auth.js (progressive enhancement, inline
errors, no-JS fallback).

